    tests+stdlib: dispatch Value::Builtin; the builtin surface was unreachable
    
    stdlib::builtin_function had no caller in src/. Both engines asked
    runtime::builtin, which implements 34 names and not abs/sqrt/uppercase/
    trim, so every name registered as Value::Builtin was dispatched by
    nothing and answered "Unknown function" -- the message for a name nothing
    implements, applied to names SPEC.md documents.
    
    stdlib::builtin is now the single resolver both engines call, so a
    builtin cannot answer in the tree-walker and be missing from the bytecode
    VM. MODULES gains text and math. formats is NOT added: SPEC.md
    documented formats.parse_json and friends, none of which were ever names
    -- JSON and CSV are their own modules -- so the spec was corrected rather
    than the namespace invented.
    
    Two pre-existing tests meet at sqrt(-1): numeric_edge_test asserts
